# This tree is POSIX sh and Android sh before it is anything else: no script here
# may carry CRLF. The defect this prevents was measured, not imagined - a packer
# rewritten from Windows reached CI with CRLF and dash refused it at the block it
# had just gained ("set: Illegal option -"), while the same bytes ran perfectly in
# Git Bash, whose shell reads scripts in text mode and strips the CR. One host hid
# the defect; CI and the device would not have.
* text=auto eol=lf
